{
  "dom_id": "step-q181998",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $C=[\\sqrt{2},7]?$\n\n$min(C)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,max(C)=$\n{{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(C) & =min[\\sqrt{2},7]=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ max(C) & =max[\\sqrt{2},7]=7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
